{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_project_state_handover", "label": "Project State and Handover", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-09-21", "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_project_state_layering_contracts", "label": "Five import-linter Contracts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The layering is not a convention, it is checked in CI. The fifth contract \u2014 Kafka is an adapter \u2014 was added in Phase 2 because the thing that would quietly undo the seam is one `from aiokafka import ...` in a service."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_ports", "label": "The Seven Ports", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything crossing a layer goes through a Protocol in application/ports/. Adapters raise only the exception types the port documents, translating every driver error into StorageError (retryable) or UnprocessableEventError (permanent), so the processor asks one question: retryable?"}, {"id": "docs_project_state_consumer_progress", "label": "consumer_progress Table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PK (consumer_group, stream) with position upserted to greatest(stored, incoming). The aggregator records how far it has applied each topic-partition in the same transaction as the bars and skips anything at or below that mark. If you add a consumer that accumulates anything, nothing forces you to use this and you will reproduce the bug."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_aggregator_double_count_bug", "label": "The Bar Aggregator Redelivery Double-Count Bug", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Idempotent writes are not an idempotent consumer: the aggregator accumulates, so at-least-once redelivery doubled volume, trade_count and vwap while open/high/low/close stayed perfect and every CHECK constraint passed. The restart tests missed it because they resumed with new trades \u2014 resuming is the easy half. Caught by distrusting a '470 rows' proof that was actually un-consumed backlog, then rewinding 3,000 offsets across three partitions; every additive field came back exactly 2\u00d7. An ordinary Ctrl-C was enough to trigger it, because graceful shutdown wrote final bars without committing offsets."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_idempotent_writes_vs_consumer", "label": "Idempotent Writes \u2260 Idempotent Consumer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The guarantee holds when the write is a replacement and fails when it is an addition. A test that replays a batch is not a test of redelivery; write the test that rewinds offsets and asserts the additive fields did not move. And interrogate evidence that agrees with you \u2014 the accepted proof was measuring something else entirely."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_phase2_producer_bugs", "label": "Phase 2 Kafka Producer Bugs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A broker restart permanently poisons an idempotent producer with OutOfOrderSequenceNumber; closing a poisoned producer hangs forever because stop() flushes the very batches being refused; rebuilding left a window with no client; a poll where every record is malformed loops forever; a failed start() leaked the client. Items 2 and 3 were introduced by the fix for item 1 and found only against a real broker \u2014 the unit tests passed throughout."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_environment_traps", "label": "Environment Traps", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": ".env once pointed at a throwaway PostgreSQL in a session temp folder on port 55432 while the Compose database sat empty \u2014 check TW_DATABASE_URL before believing anything about the data. Git Bash mangles container paths (prefix MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1), and the running API holds .venv executables open so uv add fails."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_adr_index", "label": "ADR Index and Build Status", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a715", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ADRs are immutable once accepted; a decision that changes gets a new ADR superseding the old one. Two will bite whoever builds Phase 6: strategies are configuration not code, and the execution simulator is a shared library."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_rules_for_next_worker", "label": "Rules for Whoever Works on This Next", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a720", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never commit or push; creating and editing files is permitted; do not weaken a check to make it pass; ADRs are immutable; report honestly \u2014 if a test proves something narrower than it sounds like, say what it actually proves."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_recommended_next_step", "label": "Recommended Next Step", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a721", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Phase 5 is the only remaining hard prerequisite for Phase 6, because strategies, portfolios and every backtest artefact are owner-scoped in the schema and building those endpoints before auth means writing them twice. Phase 4 is the better choice if the priority is something to look at, and it is the first use of Redis, which has been running in Compose since Phase 0 with no consumer."}, {"id": "docs_project_state_pre_existing_test_bugs", "label": "Two Pre-Existing Test Bugs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "test_health asserted /ready returns 503 by assuming no database was running while pointing at the very database the README tells you to start; test_migrations built a URL from str(engine.url), which masks the password as *** and passed only against trust auth."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_project_state_handover", "target": "docs_project_state_layering_contracts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_layering_contracts", "target": "backend_readme_import_linter_layering", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_ports", "target": "architecture_ports_before_adapters", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_ports", "target": "architecture_marketdataprovider_port", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_ports", "target": "docs_pipeline_failure_classification", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "StorageError vs UnprocessableEventError", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_aggregator_double_count_bug", "target": "docs_project_state_consumer_progress", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_aggregator_double_count_bug", "target": "docs_project_state_idempotent_writes_vs_consumer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_aggregator_double_count_bug", "target": "architecture_bar_aggregator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_aggregator_double_count_bug", "target": "architecture_f7_duplicate_delivery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_idempotent_writes_vs_consumer", "target": "docs_schema_idempotency_constraints", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "\u00a719", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_project_state_idempotent_writes_vs_consumer", "target": "docs_backfill_restart_recovery", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"s